course: dictionary
lesson: 15111
title: Safeguard: keeping things and people safe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To safeguard something means to protect it from harm or danger. Safeguard can be a verb, so you can safeguard, safeguards, safeguarded or safeguarding. «A helmet safeguards your head when you ride your bike.» The helmet keeps your head safe from harm, so safeguards means protects.
explain: Safeguard can also be a noun, meaning a thing that protects. «A lock is a safeguard against thieves.» The lock is the protection, and it works against thieves. When you name the danger, use the words «safeguard against».
explain: In school, safeguarding is a serious word. «Our school has a safeguarding lead who helps keep every child safe.» It means keeping children safe from harm and abuse. Every adult at school must keep children safe and report any worry, and if you are ever worried, tell a trusted adult.
fact: Safeguard is a verb (to protect) and a noun (a protection).
fact: «Safeguard» means to protect something or someone from harm or danger.
fact: «Safeguarding» in school means keeping children safe from harm and abuse.
fact: Passwords safeguard your online accounts, and laws safeguard people's rights.
fact: Useful phrases: «safeguard against», «a safeguard for», and «safeguarding lead».
exercise: «A helmet safeguards your head when you cycle.» What does safeguards mean here? | Paints something | Makes something heavier | Breaks something | *Protects from harm
exercise: «A lock is a safeguard against thieves.» What is a safeguard? | *Something that protects you from harm | A person who steals | A loud noise | A thing that breaks easily
exercise: «Our school has a safeguarding lead.» What does safeguarding mean in school? | Teaching children to swim | Giving children extra homework | Making school lunches | *Keeping children safe from harm and abuse
test: «Passwords safeguard your online accounts.» Which word means the same as safeguard here? | *Protect | Share | Forget | Delete
test: Mum said, «Wear sun cream to ___ your skin from burning.» Which word fits best? | spoil | ignore | break | *safeguard
exam: Lucy says safeguarding just means playing games at school. What does it really mean? | Doing extra homework | Playing games at break time | Giving out prizes | *Keeping children safe from harm and abuse
